  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Where the model is — and is not",
      "items": [
        "Three model calls on the intake path: extract, embed, adjudicate.",
        "Cosine, the weighted sum and every band are deterministic code.",
        "The model proposes; only code writes to the database."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Keyless by default",
      "items": [
        "Real Gemini output was recorded once into committed fixtures and is replayed by input hash.",
        "All 56 corpus inputs are covered, so a reviewer with no key sees genuine semantic matching.",
        "Free-typed text outside the corpus falls back to n-grams and is labelled degraded in the UI.",
        "Scoring records factor estimates through Gemini only when a key is set (scripts/score.ts:161), then reads every one of them back through replay."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Untrusted request text",
      "items": [
        "Every model call returns a Zod-validated object; free text cannot become control flow.",
        "Request text goes in a delimited block, never concatenated into the instruction section.",
        "A schema violation or unknown enum resolves to distinct — the non-destructive outcome.",
        "body_raw is immutable and rendered escaped."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Two things that are not here",
      "items": [
        "No queue, no cache, no vector index: retrieval is one brute-force scan over all live problems, which is correct at this scale.",
        "No separate backend. Server Components read SQLite directly and Server Actions write; the single HTTP route exists only because the intake stream needs NDJSON."
      ]
    }
  ]
}
